=== 2026-09-05, re-scored again on further review of pull request 84 ===
Re-run of score.py against the same committed output/shares.json and
output/states_meta.json. No state was rebuilt and no decomposition was run. Two
changes to the script. First, every permutation test now starts its random number
generator from the registered seed 11011, which specification section 7.1
requires; the previous version offset the reverse-direction tests and the
secondary readings to 11012, 11013, 11014 and 11015. Second, the script now
inspects the shares file for the per-decomposition iteration-safety-bound flag
that decompose.py began writing on 2026-09-05 and refuses to score a file in
which any flag is set; the committed shares file predates the flag, so the check
reports that it cannot be applied rather than passing silently, which is the line
at the top of the run below. Effect of the seed correction: all four verdicts
unchanged (H6 NOT SUPPORTED, H16 NOT SUPPORTED, H16a NOT SUPPORTED, H16b
SUPPORTED), every supporting and refuting layer set unchanged (H16 refuted at
layers 5, 8 and 10; H16b supported at layers 5 to 9), 35 p-values moved in the
fourth decimal place and none crossed the 0.05 threshold, which was checked
explicitly by comparing the old and new verdict files entry by entry. Six numbers
quoted in RESULTS_EXP011.md moved with them and were corrected there. Running the
script twice in succession gave a byte-identical verdicts.json.
